course: dictionary
lesson: 1767
title: Clench: when the body shows a feeling
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Your body can show how you feel, and this story uses the word clench to show it. «Anger is a normal feeling, but it makes the body ready to fight: the heart beats fast, the face goes hot and the fists clench.» Clench means to press tightly together, so the fists squeeze shut.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «the fists squeeze tightly shut» still make sense? Yes, so clench fits. Other clues help too: «clenched teeth» and «clenched jaw» both describe a part of the face pressed hard together.
explain: Clench can also mean to hold something very tightly. «He stood in the office doorway with his fists still clenched» tells you Jake's hands were still shut tight, not loose and relaxed.
fact: «Clench» means to press something tightly together, or to hold something very tightly.
fact: Clenched fists, a clenched jaw and clenched teeth all show muscles squeezed hard.
fact: A red face, clenched fists or a tight jaw and a loud voice are signs of anger.
fact: People also clench their teeth when they are tense, or when they are trying hard not to cry.
fact: «Through clenched teeth» means speaking while your teeth are pressed tightly together.
exercise: «He stood in the doorway with his fists still clenched.» What does clenched mean here? | *Pressed tightly shut | Open and loose | Hidden in his pockets | Raised high to wave
exercise: A red face, clenched fists and a loud voice are signs of what? | *Anger | Sleepiness | Happiness | Surprise at a party
exercise: In PE you clench your muscles to hold a position. What does clench mean in that sentence? | Relax them completely | *Squeeze them tightly | Shake them quickly | Stretch them out wide
test: «Through clenched teeth» means you are... | Singing softly | *Speaking with your teeth pressed tightly together | Laughing loudly | Eating quickly
test: Which word is the past tense of clench? | clench | clenches | clenching | *clenched
exam: Ella says a clenched jaw means a person is sleepy. What is the best answer? | *No, clenched means pressed tightly together, so a clenched jaw is tense | No, it means the person is laughing | No, clenched means opened wide | Yes, a sleepy jaw is always clenched
